single-family finished lots to local, regional, and national homebuilders. It also leases office space. Forestar Group Inc. was incorporated in 2005 and is headquartered in Arlington, Texas. Forestar Group Inc. operates as a subsidiary of D.R. Horton, Inc.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Anthony W. Oxley | President, CEO & Executive Chairman | Age 61 | Compensation: $1.9M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 408 people. Revenue per employee of $4.0M ranks in the above the sector median among Real Estate peers, with revenue growing 18%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $709K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $18K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 0\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Forestar Group Inc is a small-cap real estate business with a $1.2B market cap on $1.6B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +4% over the past three years and +24% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory. Operating margins are contracting by -2.2pp, the first warning that competitive pressure is eroding the franchise.","Returns on capital run at 11% against a 8% cost of capital, a 3-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","The business throws off $289M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 18 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.03\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.7\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.7) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins softening -2.2pp YoY \u2014 early warning on the moat","sev":"amber","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Operating margins 11% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 5.8% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Interest-rate sensitivity and tenant-credit risk \u2014 cap rates and refinancing costs move faster than the 10-year leases can absorb.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Climate and insurance cost escalation \u2014 rising premiums and coverage withdrawals in flood/fire zones are repricing assets that the market once treated as perpetuities.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 67% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 54% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Real Estate sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 6% over 3 months"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Forestar CFO James Douglas Allen Vests 2,601 RSUs and Surrenders 963 Shares for Tax Withholding","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/forestar-cfo-james-douglas-allen-